```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "overwrite a bag's version of a tiddler with another's; both keep history"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///carriage.bag.copies"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.copies"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.bag.copies"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.bag.copies ~ the residency COPY: the destination's version gives way to the source's

`COPY` overwrites the destination bag's version of one tiddler with the source bag's; both bags keep their history, and the change-id travels with the tiddler so the copy reads as the same change in another bag. It takes the title, the source bag, the destination bag and a change-id (named, or minted when absent), and the vessel runs it as one verb-tiddler wrapped in an effect record.

A terminal asks `Proceed? [y/N]` before it submits; `yes=true` names the intent off a terminal, `mu=pentacle` previews and commits nothing, `in-wiki=true` runs the act in the active wiki's island. At bag grain the same verb grants every title the source holds in a new or existing destination (one transfer-id family audits the batch), and it carries the wiki-level crossing beside CREATE.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ copy-a-title · preview-first

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`copy-a-title` params=`title/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example from/lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/lares to/lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/lares/working ~ the destination's version takes the source's words`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`preview-first` params=`title/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example from/lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/lares to/lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/lares/working mu/pentacle ~ name the effect and commit nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ title · from · to · change-id · in-wiki · yes · mu

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`title` params=`takes/title needs/required ~ the tiddler's title (its Work-level identity)`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`from` params=`takes/bag-uri needs/required ~ the bag the tiddler leaves or reads from`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`to` params=`takes/bag-uri needs/required ~ the bag the tiddler lands in`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`change-id` params=`takes/id ~ the change's own identity, named once so a re-send reads as the same change; absent, the verb mints one`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`in-wiki` params=`~ run the act in the active wiki's island`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`yes` params=`~ the intent a call off a terminal names in place of the y/N a terminal asks`>>
<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/mu`>>
<<has entity=`cell` name=`_0` params=`mu/pentacle ~ a dry run: the island walks the act through a capturing access and names the effect it would land, committing nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel checks the writer's cap on the destination bag; a terminal asks y/N before it submits unless yes=true rides, and an agent off a terminal names yes=true`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · cap-denied · outcome-unknown

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[carriage.bag.copies title/<title> from/<bag> to/<bag>]] ~ --title, --from and --to all stand required; the line names the one missing`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`cap-denied` params=`~ the writer's cap on the destination bag falls short; nothing landed`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`outcome-unknown` params=`~ this process stopped waiting after the vessel answered; a short read found no receipt for this attempt's request id; read it back with lares vessel request <id> before any re-run`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ done · preview · refused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`done` params=`exit/0 fields/[[verb status requestId receipt]] ~ the vessel ran the action and wrote its effect record; the receipt names the outcome tiddler`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`preview` params=`exit/0 ~ with mu=pentacle the vessel names the effect it would land and commits nothing`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`refused` params=`~ the vessel refused by name (cap-denied or a verb-error); the line carries its reason and cure`>>
```

